.TH UNBOUND-DASHBOARD 1 "2026-11-14" "unbound-dashboard" "Unbound DNS Dashboard"
.SH NAME
unbound-dashboard \- lightweight real-time visualization dashboard for Unbound DNS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unbound-dashboard
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unbound-dashboard
is a lightweight, single-binary DNS visualization dashboard written in Go
with SQLite storage. It reads DNS query data from Unbound via a DNSTap unix
socket or a verbose log file, and serves a real-time web dashboard with
Top-N query, blocked/abnormal domain and response-code statistics.
.PP
The dashboard listens on 127.0.0.1:9153 by default. It exposes an HTML
dashboard, a JSON API, a Prometheus metrics endpoint and a health check.
.PP
DNSTap query and response frames are correlated into a single transaction;
every record is normalized (lowercase, no trailing dot), optionally filtered
and optionally anonymized before it reaches SQLite. Inserts are batched into
transactions. Existing v0.2.x databases are migrated automatically.
.SH DATA SOURCE MODES
Exactly one source must be specified. Use \fB\-\-test\-config\fR to validate
the configuration without opening the database or creating directories.
.SS DNSTap mode (recommended)
The dashboard creates and listens on a DNSTap Frame Streams unix socket;
Unbound connects to it as a client. Requires Unbound built with
\fB\-\-enable\-dnstap\fR. The socket is created with mode \fB0660\fR and
group \fBunbound\fR by default, never world-writable.
.SS Log file mode
Tails an Unbound verbose log file, detecting logrotate by inode change.
Requires \fBverbosity: 2\fR and \fBlog-queries: yes\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Data source
.TP
.BI \-D " \fR,\fP " \-\-dnstap " PATH"
DNSTap unix socket path. Mutually exclusive with \fB\-l\fR.
.TP
.BI \-l " \fR,\fP " \-\-log\-file " PATH"
Unbound verbose log file path. Mutually exclusive with \fB\-D\fR.
.TP
.BI \-r " \fR,\fP " \-\-log\-from\-start " BOOL"
Read the whole log file at startup. Default: true. Use
\fB\-\-log\-from\-start=false\fR to tail only new data.
.SS HTTP and storage
.TP
.BI \-a " \fR,\fP " \-\-addr " ADDRESS"
HTTP listen address. Default: \fB127.0.0.1\fR.
.TP
.BI \-p " \fR,\fP " \-\-port " PORT"
HTTP listen port. Default: \fB9153\fR.
.TP
.BI \-d " \fR,\fP " \-\-data\-dir " DIR"
SQLite database directory. Default: \fB/var/lib/unbound\fR.
.TP
.BI \-t " \fR,\fP " \-\-ttl " DAYS"
Retention in days, purged hourly. Default: \fB90\fR (1..9999).
.TP
.BI \-S " \fR,\fP " \-\-size " MB"
Maximum database size in MB. Default: \fB200\fR (1..9999).
.SS Edge transforms
.TP
.BI \-i " \fR,\fP " \-\-ignore\-domains " LIST"
Comma-separated domain suffixes dropped before storage.
.TP
.BI \-b " \fR,\fP " \-\-block\-rcodes " LIST"
Response codes counted as blocked. Default: \fBNXDOMAIN,REFUSED\fR.
Set to an empty string to count only explicit RPZ/policy signals.
NXDOMAIN is a normal negative answer, not inherently a block.
.TP
.BI \-y " \fR,\fP " \-\-dnstap\-types " LIST"
DNSTap message types admitted to the query/response merger. Default:
\fBCLIENT_QUERY,CLIENT_RESPONSE\fR.
.TP
.BI \-A " \fR,\fP " \-\-anonymize\-ip
Hash client IPs with a per-process random salt before storing them.
.SS DNSTap socket and batched writer
.TP
.BI \-m " \fR,\fP " \-\-socket\-mode " OCTAL"
Socket permissions. Default: \fB0660\fR.
.TP
.BI \-g " \fR,\fP " \-\-socket\-group " GROUP"
Group to chown the socket to. Default: \fBunbound\fR. Empty disables chown.
.TP
.BI \-q " \fR,\fP " \-\-queue\-size " N"
Ingest queue capacity. Default: \fB4096\fR. Full queue drops frames and
increments \fBrecords_dropped_total\fR.
.TP
.BI \-B " \fR,\fP " \-\-batch\-size " N"
Records per SQLite transaction. Default: \fB64\fR.
.TP
.BI \-f " \fR,\fP " \-\-flush\-ms " N"
Max delay before flushing a partial batch. Default: \fB10\fR.
.SS Other
.TP
.BI \-P " \fR,\fP " \-\-debug\-public
Allow /debug from non-loopback clients. Default: off.
.TP
.BI \-k " \fR,\fP " \-\-debug\-token " TOKEN"
Require \fBAuthorization: Bearer TOKEN\fR for /debug.
.TP
.BI \-T " \fR,\fP " \-\-test\-config
Validate configuration and exit with "config OK!".
.TP
.B \-V "\fR,\fP " \-\-version
Print the version (injected at build time) and exit.
.TP
.B \-h "\fR,\fP " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.PP
Both \fB\-\-opt value\fR and \fB\-\-opt=value\fR forms are accepted.
.SH HTTP ENDPOINTS
.TP
.B /
HTML dashboard, auto-refreshes every 5 seconds. All dynamic labels are
HTML-escaped.
.TP
.B /stats
JSON statistics: version, total_queries, blocked_queries, uptime, since,
top_queries, top_blocked and rcode_breakdown.
.TP
.B /metrics
Prometheus text exposition with pipeline counters (frames_received_total,
frames_malformed_total, records_dropped_total, records_inserted_total, ...).
.TP
.B /healthz
JSON liveness check.
.TP
.B /debug
Plain-text runtime information. Restricted to loopback unless
\fB\-\-debug\-public\fR or \fB\-\-debug\-token\fR is configured.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate then start with DNSTap:
.PP
.RS
.nf
unbound-dashboard --test-config --dnstap /var/lib/unbound/dnstap.sock
unbound-dashboard --dnstap /var/lib/unbound/dnstap.sock
.fi
.RE
.PP
Drop health-check noise and anonymize client IPs:
.PP
.RS
.nf
unbound-dashboard --dnstap /var/lib/unbound/dnstap.sock \\
    --ignore-domains arpa,internal --anonymize-ip
.fi
.RE
.PP
Strict blocking semantics (only RPZ/policy counts):
.PP
.RS
.nf
unbound-dashboard --dnstap /var/lib/unbound/dnstap.sock --block-rcodes=
.fi
.RE
.SH SYSTEMD SERVICE
After installing the .deb package, edit the unit to set your data source,
then run:
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl edit unbound-dashboard
systemctl enable --now unbound-dashboard
.fi
.RE
.PP
The service does not require root; a dedicated user with write access to
\fB/var/lib/unbound\fR is sufficient.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/unbound\-dashboard
The dashboard binary.
.TP
.I /var/lib/unbound/dashboard.db
SQLite database (default location).
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/unbound\-dashboard.service
Systemd service unit.
